Approach :
- Take the levels passed by both players (ignoring the first count value) and combine them into one list.
- Convert the combined list into a set to remove duplicates and check if its length equals max_level.


CODE :

def levels(max_level):
    k=list(map(int, input().split()))
    l=list(map(int, input().split()))
    
    if (len(set(k[1:] + l[1:])) == max_level):
        print("I become the guy.")
    else:
        print("Oh, my keyboard!")
    
max_level=int(input())
levels(max_level)
